1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
The Konya Closed Basin has 739 recorded sinkholes. Groundwater has dropped about 30 metres since the 1980s.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:15,000
This is the basin's total water storage. The trend is down.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:30,000
The same crisis is unfolding in California's Central Valley, in Punjab and in the Murray-Darling. BasinShift runs in all four.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Meet Mehmet. He farms 12 irrigated hectares in Çumra. Sugar beet in 2025, maize in 2026, and he plans beet again.

5
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Under the 2026 rule, his plan risks a red card and the loss of all support payments.

6
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:05,000
BasinShift stress-tested more than 20,000 four-year plans against 40 years of weather.

7
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:15,000
The Balance plan uses [ ] cubic metres less water per decare each year and keeps [ ] lira of support.

8
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Every card explains why it was suggested, the evidence, the gaps, and what to check locally.

9
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:30,000
What if rainfall drops by 20 percent? The plans are recalculated at once.

10
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:38,000
What is right for one farmer can become a sinkhole when a thousand farmers do it.

11
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:45,000
A coordinated basin plan stays within the water budget. One extra cubic metre of water is worth [ ] lira to the basin.

12
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:52,000
The one-page scorecard is for banks, insurers and cooperatives.

13
00:01:52,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Every dataset is labelled real or synthetic. Banks are stress-tested. Now fields are too.
